Reproduction run, 2026-08-01 — everything in this lab rebuilt from scratch and re-measured
on the board after it was reimaged. Fresh llama.cpp (a7a6d0d, ~6 weeks newer than the
original 91d2fc3), fresh cross-build via build-aarch64.sh, models re-fetched.

Differs from the 2026-07-20 runs in one way: the desktop was left running (sddm at the
greeter, board otherwise idle) rather than stopped, so these are "quiet but not quiesced".

| model                          |       size |     params | backend    | threads |            test |                  t/s |
| ------------------------------ | ---------: | ---------: | ---------- | ------: | --------------: | -------------------: |
| qwen2 1B Q4_K - Medium         | 373.71 MiB |   494.03 M | CPU        |       6 |            pp64 |         41.89 ± 0.16 |
| qwen2 1B Q4_K - Medium         | 373.71 MiB |   494.03 M | CPU        |       6 |            tg64 |         18.02 ± 0.07 |
| qwen2 1B Q4_0                  | 330.95 MiB |   494.03 M | CPU        |       6 |            pp64 |        128.95 ± 3.65 |
| qwen2 1B Q4_0                  | 330.95 MiB |   494.03 M | CPU        |       6 |            tg64 |         22.75 ± 0.39 |

vs bench-05-quant-sweep-clean.log (2026-07-20, fully quiesced):

              pp64            tg64
  Q4_K_M      40.75 -> 41.89   17.66 -> 18.02
  Q4_0       148.94 -> 128.95  23.77 -> 22.75

Q4_K_M lands within 3%. Q4_0 prompt processing is 13% below the quiesced number — the
cost of leaving the desktop up, and consistent with prefill being the compute-bound half.
The finding is unchanged: Q4_0 is 3.1x prompt and +26% generation over Q4_K_M here.

